    "description": "Republic of Ireland District Electoral Divisions/Wards as at 1946-07-15, assembled from Connacht (= 1919 boundaries), Leinster 1946, Munster (= 1944 boundaries), Ulster (= 1921 boundaries). Modified version of District Electoral Divisions/Wards 1950. In 1950, the new DED of Limerick Rural was formed out of parts of Limerick North Rural and Limerick South Rural due to the forthcoming expansion of Limerick county borough. Also relevant is the renaming of the following DEDs between 1936 Census Reports Volume 1 (published 1938) and 1946 Census Reports Volume 1 (published 1949): Edgeworthstown to Meathas Truim (Longford), Drumcondra to Drumconrath (Meath), Philipstown to Daingean (Offaly), Charleville to Rathluirc (Cork), Shanballymore to Shanballymore Town (Cork)",
